Declare the two no-argument callbacks with C prototypes.

Source: CarbonHeaders-18.1 (214a9ae7ab3c0c78ddb50328ca226e6313c4c782), MacTypes.h.
Scope: macOS SDK 26.5, arm64 and x86_64.

Local compatibility derivation using the existing Apple typedefs. Using void
keeps valid no-argument calls and makes the compiler reject extra arguments.
The paired C11 probes agree with the reference SDK on both architectures.

Evidence: .agents/skills/review-macos-c-sdk/scripts/sdk_review/headers/data/macosx26.5/tested-header-repairs.md.

--- a/usr/include/MacTypes.h
+++ b/usr/include/MacTypes.h
@@ -310,8 +310,8 @@
         UniversalProcHandle     Pointer to a UniversalProcPtr
         
 *********************************************************************************/
-typedef CALLBACK_API_C( long , ProcPtr )();
-typedef CALLBACK_API( void , Register68kProcPtr )();
+typedef CALLBACK_API_C( long , ProcPtr )(void);
+typedef CALLBACK_API( void , Register68kProcPtr )(void);
 #if TARGET_RT_MAC_CFM
 /*  The RoutineDescriptor structure is defined in MixedMode.h */
 typedef struct RoutineDescriptor *UniversalProcPtr;
